      "checks": {
        "degree_identity": "2026-2027 Artificial Intelligence Major, BS in Engineering; McCormick degree, separate from secondary-major variants.",
        "required_and_choices": "Actual major and college tables establish 13 fixed records after applying the published corresponding honors-calculus substitute; discrete mathematics remains fixed. Introductory programming and engineering programming remain separate choices. Four advanced electives now have choice ancestry; all 14 introductory exceptions remain eligible alongside the open 300-level-or-higher rule. Five distinct breadth domains out of six, one societal-impact choice and seven technical electives remain separate; science lecture/lab and writing/design bundles are intact.",
        "elective_pools": "Read all ten major tables, four college core tables, two public theme tables and governing prose. Thirteen finite additional theme exceptions are now mapped alongside open eligible-department predicates, specific exclusions, GEOG 1xx and credit-bearing 300-level PRDV. No finite catalog is invented for open level/department rules. ES_APPM 252-2 remains contextual to the generic honors sequence, not another fixed AI obligation.",
        "prerequisites": "Reviewed all available exact course blocks, including graduate entries and sixteen generic special-topic descriptions. Published preparation, graduate permission, home-school restrictions, concurrency, repeats and credit exclusions remain exact. COMP_SCI 212 names 110/111 while the introductory degree slot permits 180/111: possible extra preparation is not a universal requirement or automatic waiver. MATH 230-2 excludes McCormick students despite appearing in the major introductory exception list; its availability is conditional on student route/prior credit/approval, not assumed for every McCormick student. No instructor permission or transfer approval is guaranteed.",
        "credits_and_units": "Actual directories corroborate source units, including 0.5 writing/design and 0.34 laboratory amounts. No quarter-hour conversion. Five scalar amounts remain unknown: the AP/IB transfer-credit designation and four code-only GEOG exceptions. The theme combines fractional units, so its finite pool is represented under seven units rather than seven extra courses. Lecture/lab pairs count their actual amounts and obey course restrictions.",
        "classification": "All 190 source records have explicit reviews:169 descriptions or previously reviewed core summaries,16 limited topic-title observations, one unclassified examination-credit designation and 4 unclassified GEOG code-only listings. Actual descriptions distinguish systems from software foundations, domain science from AI methods, human implications from AI methods, and genuinely mixed content. Current profile:13 fixed,175 option identities,1 contextual honors identity. One explicit robotics cross-list reconciles 2 source records; other level variants, alternatives and credit exclusions remain separate.",
        "family_composition": "No family inheritance. This is the standalone McCormick BSE pathway; separate additional-major variants are not changed or certified.",
        "degree_wide_requirements": "Reread 2026–2027 college requirements and policies, university registration requirement, public theme/FAQ, registration, duplicate-course sets, transfer procedures, P/N page and linked 2018PDF. Confirmed 48total/26 core/22 major, GPA2.0, at most 3 D major units, C external credit,4 major-transfer-unit cap,11 unique major units, residency and petition rules. Substantive current-catalog versus undated-public P/N/theme discrepancies remain unresolved and prevent full-degree policy certification. Other-home-school degrees are outside this record, not missing McCormick obligations."
